<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jehoram of Judah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a> · Also known as Joram of Judah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jehoram was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> in the mid-9th century BCE, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehoshaphat">Jehoshaphat</a>. His marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athaliah">Athaliah</a>, daughter of the house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omri">Omri</a>, sealed the alliance with Israel. According to the Bible, Edom and the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libnah">Libnah</a> revolted against him, and Judah lost control of Edom for decades. His son Ahaziah succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jehoram-of-judah.jpg" alt="Jehoram of Judah" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume Rouille · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jehoram_of_Judah.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
